#. type: Yaml Front Matter Hash Value: description
#, no-wrap
msgid "IBM Quantum Composer is a graphical programming tool. Drag and drop operations to build circuits and run them on quantum hardware."
msgstr "IBM Quantum Composer ialah alat pengaturcaraan grafik. Seret dan lepas operasi untuk membina Circuit dan jalankannya pada perkakasan kuantum."

#. type: Yaml Front Matter Hash Value: title
#, no-wrap
msgid "IBM Quantum Composer"
msgstr "IBM Quantum Composer"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "{/* cspell:ignore gatename, ungroup, ungrouping */}\n"
msgstr "{/* cspell:ignore gatename, ungroup, ungrouping */}\n"

#. type: Title #
#, no-wrap
msgid "IBM Quantum Composer {#ibm-quantum-composer}"
msgstr "IBM Quantum Composer {#ibm-quantum-composer}"

#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "What is it? {#what-is-it}"
msgstr "Apa itu? {#what-is-it}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "[IBM Quantum&reg; Composer](https://quantum.cloud.ibm.com/composer) is a graphical quantum programming tool that lets you drag and drop operations to build quantum circuits and run them on quantum hardware.\n"
msgstr "[IBM Quantum&reg; Composer](https://quantum.cloud.ibm.com/composer) ialah alat pengaturcaraan kuantum berasaskan grafik yang membolehkan anda seret dan lepas operasi untuk membina Circuit kuantum dan menjalankannya pada perkakasan kuantum.\n"

#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "What can it do? {#what-can-it-do}"
msgstr "Apa yang boleh ia lakukan? {#what-can-it-do}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Visualize qubit states**\n"
msgstr "**Gambaran visual keadaan qubit**\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "See how changes to your circuit affect the state of qubits, shown as an interactive q-sphere, or histograms showing measurement probabilities or statevector simulations.\n"
msgstr "Lihat bagaimana perubahan pada Circuit anda mempengaruhi keadaan qubit, ditunjukkan sebagai q-sphere interaktif, atau histogram yang memaparkan kebarangkalian pengukuran atau simulasi statevector.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Run on quantum hardware**\n"
msgstr "**Jalankan pada perkakasan kuantum**\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Run your circuits on real quantum hardware to understand the effects of device noise.\n"
msgstr "Jalankan Circuit anda pada perkakasan kuantum sebenar untuk memahami kesan hingar peranti.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Automatically generate code**\n"
msgstr "**Jana kod secara automatik**\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Instead of writing code by hand, automatically generate OpenQASM or Python code that behaves the same way as the circuit you created with the Composer.\n"
msgstr "Daripada menulis kod secara manual, jana kod OpenQASM atau Python secara automatik yang berkelakuan sama seperti Circuit yang anda cipta dengan Composer.\n"

#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Tour of the interface {#tour-of-the-interface}"
msgstr "Lawatan antara muka {#tour-of-the-interface}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "IBM Quantum Composer has a customizable set of tools that allow you to build, visualize, and run quantum circuits on quantum processing units (QPUs). Use the \"More options\" menu on each window to access additional tools and actions.\n"
msgstr "IBM Quantum Composer mempunyai set alat yang boleh disesuaikan untuk membolehkan anda membina, menggambarkan, dan menjalankan Circuit kuantum pada unit pemprosesan kuantum (QPU). Gunakan menu \"More options\" pada setiap tetingkap untuk mengakses alat dan tindakan tambahan.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "![IBM Quantum Composer window](/docs/images/guides/composer/composer-annotation.svg)\n"
msgstr "![Tetingkap IBM Quantum Composer.](/docs/images/guides/composer/composer-annotation.svg)\n"

#. type: Bullet: '1. '
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Operations catalog** - These are the building blocks of quantum circuits. Drag and drop these gates and other operations onto the graphical circuit editor. Different types of gates are grouped together by color. For example, classical gates are dark blue, phase gates are light blue, and non-unitary operations are grey.\n"
msgstr "**Katalog operasi** - Ini ialah blok pembinaan Circuit kuantum. Seret dan lepas gate dan operasi lain ke dalam editor Circuit grafik. Jenis gate yang berbeza dikumpulkan mengikut warna. Contohnya, gate klasik berwarna biru gelap, gate fasa berwarna biru muda, dan operasi bukan-unitari berwarna kelabu.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "   To learn about the available gates and operations, right-click an operation and select Info to read its definition.\n"
msgstr "   Untuk mengetahui tentang gate dan operasi yang tersedia, klik kanan operasi dan pilih Info untuk membaca takrifannya.\n"

#. type: Bullet: '2. '
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Code editor** - Use the View menu to open or close the code editor, which allows you to view the OpenQASM or Qiskit code for the circuit. You can edit the OpenQASM code; the Qiskit code is read-only.\n"
msgstr "**Editor kod** - Gunakan menu View untuk membuka atau menutup editor kod, yang membolehkan anda melihat kod OpenQASM atau Qiskit bagi Circuit tersebut. Anda boleh mengedit kod OpenQASM; kod Qiskit adalah baca sahaja.\n"

#. type: Bullet: '3. '
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Graphical circuit editor** - This is where you build a circuit. Drag gates and other operations onto the horizontal qubit “wires” that make up your quantum register.\n"
msgstr "**Editor Circuit grafik** - Di sinilah anda membina Circuit. Seret gate dan operasi lain ke atas \"wayar\" Qubit mengufuk yang membentuk daftar kuantum anda.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "   To remove a gate from a wire, select the gate and click the trash can icon.\n"
msgstr "   Untuk membuang gate daripada wayar, pilih gate tersebut dan klik ikon tong sampah.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "   To edit the parameters and settings on gates that support editing, select the gate on the graphical editor and click Edit.\n"
msgstr "   Untuk mengedit parameter dan tetapan pada gate yang menyokong penyuntingan, pilih gate pada editor grafik dan klik Edit.\n"

#. type: Bullet: '4. '
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Toolbar** - Access frequently used tools to undo and redo actions, change the gate alignment, and switch to inspect mode. With inspect mode, you see a step-by-step view of the qubit states as you circuit computation evolves. To learn more, see [Inspect your circuit, step-by-step](#4-inspect-your-circuit-step-by-step).\n"
msgstr "**Bar alat** - Akses alat yang kerap digunakan untuk buat asal dan buat semula tindakan, tukar penjajaran gate, dan beralih ke mod semak. Dengan mod semak, anda dapat melihat pandangan langkah demi langkah bagi keadaan qubit semasa pengiraan Circuit anda berkembang. Untuk mengetahui lebih lanjut, lihat [Semak Circuit anda, langkah demi langkah](#4-inspect-your-circuit-step-by-step).\n"

#. type: Bullet: '5. '
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Phase disks** - The phase of the qubit state vector in the complex plane is given by the line that extends from the center of the diagram to the edge of the gray disk (which rotates counterclockwise around the center point).\n"
msgstr "**Cakera fasa** - Fasa vektor keadaan qubit dalam satah kompleks diberikan oleh garis yang memanjang dari pusat diagram ke tepi cakera kelabu (yang berputar berlawanan arah jam di sekitar titik pusat).\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "    Use the View menu to show or hide the phase disks.\n"
msgstr "    Gunakan menu View untuk menunjukkan atau menyembunyikan cakera fasa.\n"

#. type: Bullet: '6. '
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Visualizations** - Visualizations characterize your circuit as you build it. They use a single-shot statevector simulator, which is different from the QPU specified in the \"Run circuit\" settings. Note that the visualizations ignore any measurement operations you add. Sign in and click **Run circuit** to get results from the specified backend instead.\n"
msgstr "**Gambaran visual** - Gambaran visual mencirikan Circuit anda semasa anda membinanya. Ia menggunakan simulator statevector satu tembakan, yang berbeza daripada QPU yang ditetapkan dalam tetapan \"Run circuit\". Ambil perhatian bahawa gambaran visual mengabaikan sebarang operasi pengukuran yang anda tambahkan. Log masuk dan klik **Run circuit** untuk mendapatkan keputusan daripada Backend yang ditetapkan.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "   Learn more in the [Visualizations](#visualizations) section.\n"
msgstr "   Ketahui lebih lanjut dalam bahagian [Gambaran visual](#visualizations).\n"

#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Build, edit, and inspect quantum circuits {#build-edit-and-inspect-quantum-circuits}"
msgstr "Bina, edit, dan semak Circuit kuantum {#build-edit-and-inspect-quantum-circuits}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "<Admonition type=\"warning\" title=\"Download your circuit files before exiting the Composer\">\n"
msgstr "<Admonition type=\"warning\" title=\"Muat turun fail Circuit anda sebelum keluar daripada Composer\">\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"If you want to continue working with a circuit at a later time, be sure to download your circuit file and store it locally before exiting your current Composer session. Use the \"Save file\" link in the upper-right corner, or go to the File menu and choose \"Save file\". When you are ready to work with the circuit again, go to the File menu and choose \"Upload .qasm file\", then navigate to your circuit file on your local drive and click Open.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"
msgstr ""
"Jika anda ingin terus bekerja dengan Circuit pada masa hadapan, pastikan anda memuat turun fail Circuit dan menyimpannya secara setempat sebelum keluar daripada sesi Composer semasa. Gunakan pautan \"Save file\" di penjuru kanan atas, atau pergi ke menu File dan pilih \"Save file\". Apabila anda bersedia untuk bekerja dengan Circuit semula, pergi ke menu File dan pilih \"Upload .qasm file\", kemudian navigasi ke fail Circuit anda pada pemacu setempat dan klik Open.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"

#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "1. Open IBM Quantum Composer {#1-open-ibm-quantum-composer}"
msgstr "1. Buka IBM Quantum Composer {#1-open-ibm-quantum-composer}"

#. type: Bullet: '1. '
#, no-wrap
msgid "(Optional) If you are not currently signed in to IBM Quantum, select **Sign in** in the upper right corner. Then, you can either sign in or **Create an IBM Cloud account**.\n"
msgstr "(Pilihan) Jika anda belum log masuk ke IBM Quantum, pilih **Sign in** di penjuru kanan atas. Kemudian, anda boleh log masuk atau **Create an IBM Cloud account**.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<Admonition type=\"note\">\n"
"   If you don’t sign in, the visualizations automatically show simulated results for up to four qubits. If you want to run your circuit on a quantum computer, or if you want to visualize a circuit that has more than four qubits, you must sign in.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"
msgstr ""
"<Admonition type=\"note\">\n"
"   Jika anda tidak log masuk, gambaran visual akan secara automatik menunjukkan keputusan simulasi untuk sehingga empat qubit. Jika anda ingin menjalankan Circuit pada komputer kuantum, atau jika anda ingin menggambarkan Circuit yang mempunyai lebih daripada empat qubit, anda perlu log masuk.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"

#. type: Bullet: '2. '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Open IBM Quantum Composer by clicking the link on the [Learning page](/learning) navigation. The workspace displays an untitled empty circuit. You can either create a new circuit, or upload a .qasm file to continue working with with a circuit you've already created. \n"
msgstr "Buka IBM Quantum Composer dengan mengklik pautan pada navigasi [halaman Pembelajaran](/learning). Ruang kerja memaparkan Circuit kosong tanpa nama. Anda boleh sama ada mencipta Circuit baharu, atau memuat naik fail .qasm untuk meneruskan kerja dengan Circuit yang telah anda cipta.\n"

#. type: Bullet: '3. '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Name your circuit by clicking on the words **Untitled circuit** and typing in a name for your circuit. Click the checkmark to save the name.\n"
msgstr "Namakan Circuit anda dengan mengklik perkataan **Untitled circuit** dan taip nama untuk Circuit anda. Klik tanda semak untuk menyimpan nama.\n"

#. type: Bullet: '4. '
#, no-wrap
msgid "(Optional) Customize your workspace:\n"
msgstr "(Pilihan) Sesuaikan ruang kerja anda:\n"

#. type: Bullet: '   * '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Use the **View** menu to change from the default theme to a monochrome theme. You can also select which panels to include on your workspace, then use the menu in the right corner of any panel to access options for further customization. The options to show or hide phase disks, choose the alignment of the qubits on your circuit, and reset the workspace to the default are in the View menu as well.\n"
msgstr "Gunakan menu **View** untuk menukar daripada tema lalai kepada tema monokrom. Anda juga boleh memilih panel yang hendak disertakan dalam ruang kerja, kemudian gunakan menu di penjuru kanan mana-mana panel untuk mengakses pilihan penyesuaian lanjut. Pilihan untuk menunjukkan atau menyembunyikan cakera fasa, memilih penjajaran qubit pada Circuit, dan menetapkan semula ruang kerja ke lalai turut terdapat dalam menu View.\n"

#. type: Bullet: '   * '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Switch between dark and light workspace themes in the bottom-right corner of the footer.\n"
msgstr "Beralih antara tema ruang kerja gelap dan cerah di penjuru kanan bawah pengaki.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "To build a circuit, you can either [drag and drop operations](#2-build-your-circuit-with-drag-and-drop), or you can enter [OpenQASM code](#3-build-your-circuit-with-openqasm-code) into the code editor.\n"
msgstr "Untuk membina Circuit, anda boleh sama ada [seret dan lepas operasi](#2-build-your-circuit-with-drag-and-drop), atau masukkan [kod OpenQASM](#3-build-your-circuit-with-openqasm-code) ke dalam editor kod.\n"

#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "2. Build your circuit with drag-and-drop {#2-build-your-circuit-with-drag-and-drop}"
msgstr "2. Bina Circuit anda dengan seret dan lepas {#2-build-your-circuit-with-drag-and-drop}"

#. type: Title ####
#, no-wrap
msgid "Operations catalog {#operations-catalog}"
msgstr "Katalog operasi {#operations-catalog}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Drag and drop operations from the operations catalog onto the quantum and classical registers. Click the search icon and enter a term in the search bar to quickly find an operation.\n"
msgstr "Seret dan lepas operasi daripada katalog operasi ke atas daftar kuantum dan klasik. Klik ikon carian dan masukkan istilah dalam bar carian untuk mencari operasi dengan cepat.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Collapse and expand the operations catalog by clicking the icon in the upper right corner of the operations panel. Click the icon next to it to toggle between a grid and list view of the catalog.\n"
msgstr "Runtuhkan dan kembangkan katalog operasi dengan mengklik ikon di penjuru kanan atas panel operasi. Klik ikon di sebelahnya untuk bertukar antara paparan grid dan senarai katalog.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Right-click an operation icon and select Info to view the definition of an operation, along with its QASM reference.\n"
msgstr "Klik kanan ikon operasi dan pilih Info untuk melihat takrifan operasi, bersama dengan rujukan QASM-nya.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "To undo or redo, use the curved arrows in the toolbar.\n"
msgstr "Untuk buat asal atau buat semula, gunakan anak panah melengkung dalam bar alat.\n"

#. type: Title ####
#, no-wrap
msgid "Alignment {#alignment}"
msgstr "Penjajaran {#alignment}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Choose Freeform alignment to place operations anywhere on the circuit. For a more compact view of your circuit, choose Left alignment. To see the order in which operations will execute, choose Layers alignment, which will apply left alignment and add column delineators that indicate the execution order, from left to right and top to bottom.\n"
msgstr "Pilih penjajaran Freeform untuk meletakkan operasi di mana sahaja dalam Circuit. Untuk paparan Circuit yang lebih padat, pilih penjajaran Left. Untuk melihat urutan pelaksanaan operasi, pilih penjajaran Layers, yang akan menerapkan penjajaran kiri dan menambah pemisah lajur yang menunjukkan urutan pelaksanaan, dari kiri ke kanan dan atas ke bawah.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Once operations are placed on your circuit, you can continue to drag and drop them to new positions.\n"
msgstr "Setelah operasi diletakkan pada Circuit anda, anda masih boleh menyeret dan melepaskannya ke kedudukan baharu.\n"

#. type: Title ####
#, no-wrap
msgid "Copy and paste {#copy-and-paste}"
msgstr "Salin dan tampal {#copy-and-paste}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Click an operation and use the icons in the contextual menu to copy and paste it.\n"
msgstr "Klik operasi dan gunakan ikon dalam menu kontekstual untuk menyalin dan menampalnya.\n"

#. type: Title ####
#, no-wrap
msgid "Select multiple operations {#select-multiple-operations}"
msgstr "Pilih beberapa operasi {#select-multiple-operations}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "You can select several operations to copy and paste them, drag them to a new location, or group them into a custom unitary operation that displays in your operations catalog and functions as a single gate.\n"
msgstr "Anda boleh memilih beberapa operasi untuk menyalin dan menampalnya, menyeretnya ke lokasi baharu, atau mengelompokkannya menjadi operasi unitari tersuai yang muncul dalam katalog operasi anda dan berfungsi sebagai satu gate tunggal.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "To select more than one operation, place your cursor just outside one of the operations, then click and drag across the area to select. Shift-click individual operations to select or deselect them. A dashed line outlines the set of operations you are selecting, and each operation that is actually part of the selection is outlined in blue.\n"
msgstr "Untuk memilih lebih daripada satu operasi, letakkan kursor anda tepat di luar salah satu operasi, kemudian klik dan seret merentasi kawasan untuk memilih. Shift-klik operasi individu untuk memilih atau menyahpilihnya. Garis putus-putus menggariskan set operasi yang anda pilih, dan setiap operasi yang benar-benar merupakan sebahagian daripada pilihan digariskan dengan warna biru.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "For example, in the following image, the Hadamard gate on q1 and the CX gate are selected. The Hadamard gate on q0 is not selected.\n"
msgstr "Sebagai contoh, dalam imej berikut, gate Hadamard pada q1 dan gate CX dipilih. Gate Hadamard pada q0 tidak dipilih.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "![A set of selected operations](/docs/images/guides/composer/3c5c063d-b15f-43cb-bb65-9728187454d8.avif)\n"
msgstr "![Set operasi yang dipilih.](/docs/images/guides/composer/3c5c063d-b15f-43cb-bb65-9728187454d8.avif)\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Select Copy from the contextual menu to copy the group.\n"
msgstr "Pilih Copy daripada menu kontekstual untuk menyalin kumpulan tersebut.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "To paste the group of operations, right-click in the circuit and select Paste.\n"
msgstr "Untuk menampal kumpulan operasi, klik kanan dalam Circuit dan pilih Paste.\n"

#. type: Title ####
#, no-wrap
msgid "Build a custom operation using the group feature {#build-a-custom-operation-using-the-group-feature}"
msgstr "Bina operasi tersuai menggunakan ciri kumpulan {#build-a-custom-operation-using-the-group-feature}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "To group several operations together and save them as a custom operation, first select the operations as described above, then select Group from the contextual menu. You are prompted to name the custom operation or you can accept the default name. Click OK, and the custom operation will be represented by a single box, both in your circuit and in the operations catalog.\n"
msgstr "Untuk mengelompokkan beberapa operasi bersama dan menyimpannya sebagai operasi tersuai, mula-mula pilih operasi seperti yang diterangkan di atas, kemudian pilih Group daripada menu kontekstual. Anda akan diminta untuk menamakan operasi tersuai atau anda boleh menerima nama lalai. Klik OK, dan operasi tersuai akan diwakili oleh satu kotak, dalam Circuit anda dan dalam katalog operasi.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "You can now drag and drop the new operation throughout your circuit. Note that the operation is saved to this circuit but does not appear in the operations catalog for other circuits.\n"
msgstr "Anda kini boleh menyeret dan melepaskan operasi baharu ke seluruh Circuit anda. Perhatikan bahawa operasi disimpan dalam Circuit ini tetapi tidak muncul dalam katalog operasi untuk Circuit lain.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "You can also build a custom operation directly in the OpenQASM code editor; see [Create a custom operation in OpenQASM](#create-a-custom-operation-in-openqasm) for more information.\n"
msgstr "Anda juga boleh membina operasi tersuai terus dalam editor kod OpenQASM; lihat [Cipta operasi tersuai dalam OpenQASM](#create-a-custom-operation-in-openqasm) untuk maklumat lanjut.\n"

#. type: Title ####
#, no-wrap
msgid "Ungroup a custom or predefined operation {#ungroup-a-custom-or-predefined-operation}"
msgstr "Nyahkumpul operasi tersuai atau pra-takrifan {#ungroup-a-custom-or-predefined-operation}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "To ungroup the gates within a custom or predefined operation, click the operation on the Composer and select Ungroup from the contextual menu. You can now move the separate operations individually. When you ungroup an operation, each element in the former group executes independently, which may mean they execute in a different order from when they were grouped together.\n"
msgstr "Untuk menyahkumpul gate dalam operasi tersuai atau pra-takrifan, klik operasi pada Composer dan pilih Ungroup daripada menu kontekstual. Anda kini boleh menggerakkan operasi yang berasingan secara individu. Apabila anda menyahkumpul operasi, setiap elemen dalam kumpulan terdahulu dilaksanakan secara bebas, yang mungkin bermakna ia dilaksanakan dalam urutan yang berbeza daripada ketika ia dikumpulkan bersama.\n"

#. type: Title ####
#, no-wrap
msgid "Expand an operation’s definition {#expand-an-operations-definition}"
msgstr "Kembangkan takrifan operasi {#expand-an-operations-definition}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "To view the operations that constitute a custom or predefined operation without ungrouping them, click **Expand definition** from the contextual menu to see the defining gates. Click the icon again to collapse the definition.\n"
msgstr "Untuk melihat operasi yang membentuk operasi tersuai atau pra-takrifan tanpa menyahkumpulkannya, klik **Expand definition** daripada menu kontekstual untuk melihat gate penentu. Klik ikon sekali lagi untuk meruntuhkan takrifan.\n"

#. type: Title ####
#, no-wrap
msgid "Rename or delete a custom operation {#rename-or-delete-a-custom-operation}"
msgstr "Namakan semula atau padam operasi tersuai {#rename-or-delete-a-custom-operation}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "To rename or delete a custom operation, right-click the operation in the operations catalog and select Rename or Delete. Deleting a custom operation from the operations catalog also deletes any instances of it on your circuit.\n"
msgstr "Untuk menamakan semula atau memadam operasi tersuai, klik kanan operasi dalam katalog operasi dan pilih Rename atau Delete. Memadamkan operasi tersuai daripada katalog operasi turut memadam semua instans operasi tersebut pada Circuit anda.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Deleting a custom operation from the circuit itself does not delete it from the operations catalog; you can only delete a custom operation from the catalog by using right-click and selecting Delete.\n"
msgstr "Memadamkan operasi tersuai daripada Circuit itu sendiri tidak memadamkannya daripada katalog operasi; anda hanya boleh memadam operasi tersuai daripada katalog dengan menggunakan klik kanan dan memilih Delete.\n"

#. type: Title ####
#, no-wrap
msgid "Add or remove registers {#add-or-remove-registers}"
msgstr "Tambah atau buang daftar {#add-or-remove-registers}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "To add or remove quantum or classical registers, click Edit → Manage registers. You can increase or decrease the number of qubits or bits in your circuit and rename the registers. Click **Ok** to apply the changes. You can also simply click the register name (e.g., `q[0]`) and use the options in the contextual menu to quickly add or delete registers or qubits.\n"
msgstr "Untuk menambah atau membuang daftar kuantum atau klasik, klik Edit → Manage registers. Anda boleh menambah atau mengurangkan bilangan qubit atau bit dalam Circuit anda dan menamakan semula daftar. Klik **Ok** untuk menerapkan perubahan. Anda juga boleh klik nama daftar (contohnya, `q[0]`) dan gunakan pilihan dalam menu kontekstual untuk menambah atau memadam daftar atau qubit dengan cepat.\n"

#. type: Title ####
#, no-wrap
msgid "Add a conditional {#add-a-conditional}"
msgstr "Tambah syarat bersyarat {#add-a-conditional}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "To add a conditional to a gate, drag the `if` operation to the gate and set the parameters in the Edit operation panel that automatically opens. You can also double-click a gate to access the Edit operation panel, and set the conditional parameters that way.\n"
msgstr "Untuk menambah syarat bersyarat pada gate, seret operasi `if` ke gate dan tetapkan parameter dalam panel Edit operation yang terbuka secara automatik. Anda juga boleh klik dua kali gate untuk mengakses panel Edit operation, dan tetapkan parameter bersyarat dengan cara itu.\n"

#. type: Title ####
#, no-wrap
msgid "Add a control modifier {#add-a-control-modifier}"
msgstr "Tambah pengubah kawalan {#add-a-control-modifier}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "A control modifier yields a gate whose original operation is now contingent on the state of the control qubit. For more details, right-click the control modifier symbol in the operations catalog, then click Info.\n"
msgstr "Pengubah kawalan menghasilkan gate yang operasi asalnya kini bergantung kepada keadaan qubit kawalan. Untuk butiran lanjut, klik kanan simbol pengubah kawalan dalam katalog operasi, kemudian klik Info.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Drag the control modifier to a gate in order to add a control to it. A dot appears on the control qubit and a line connects it to the target qubit. To edit which qubit is the control or target, click the gate and select the Edit operation icon (or double-click the gate) to open the Edit operation panel, then specify your parameters. From the Edit operation panel, you can also remove a control from a qubit by clicking the x next to the qubit name.\n"
msgstr "Seret pengubah kawalan ke gate untuk menambah kawalan padanya. Titik muncul pada qubit kawalan dan satu garis menghubungkannya ke qubit sasaran. Untuk mengedit qubit yang menjadi kawalan atau sasaran, klik gate dan pilih ikon Edit operation (atau klik dua kali gate) untuk membuka panel Edit operation, kemudian tentukan parameter anda. Daripada panel Edit operation, anda juga boleh membuang kawalan daripada qubit dengan mengklik x di sebelah nama qubit.\n"

#. type: Title ####
#, no-wrap
msgid "Visualize with phase disks throughout your circuit {#visualize-with-phase-disks-throughout-your-circuit}"
msgstr "Gambaran visual dengan cakera fasa sepanjang Circuit anda {#visualize-with-phase-disks-throughout-your-circuit}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "To visualize the state of all qubits at any point in your circuit, drag the phase disk icon from the operations catalog and place it anywhere in your circuit. A column of barrier operations and a column of phase disks are added (one barrier operation and phase disk per qubit). Hover over each phase disk to read the state of the qubit at that point in the circuit. Note that adding the phase disks does not alter your circuit; they are merely a visualization tool.\n"
msgstr "Untuk menggambarkan keadaan semua qubit pada mana-mana titik dalam Circuit anda, seret ikon cakera fasa daripada katalog operasi dan letakkannya di mana sahaja dalam Circuit anda. Satu lajur operasi penghalang dan satu lajur cakera fasa ditambahkan (satu operasi penghalang dan satu cakera fasa bagi setiap qubit). Layangkan tetikus ke atas setiap cakera fasa untuk membaca keadaan qubit pada titik tersebut dalam Circuit. Perhatikan bahawa menambahkan cakera fasa tidak mengubah Circuit anda; ia hanyalah alat gambaran visual semata-mata.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Read more about the [phase disk visualization](#phase-disk).\n"
msgstr "Baca lebih lanjut tentang gambaran visual cakera fasa [di sini.](#phase-disk)\n"

#. type: Title ####
#, no-wrap
msgid "Export a circuit image {#export-a-circuit-image}"
msgstr "Eksport imej Circuit {#export-a-circuit-image}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "To export an image of your circuit, select File → Export circuit image. The Export options window opens, where you can choose a theme (light, dark, white on black, or black on white), a format (.svg or .png), and whether you want to apply a line wrap. After you’ve chosen your options, click Export.\n"
msgstr "Untuk mengeksport imej Circuit anda, pilih File → Export circuit image. Tetingkap pilihan eksport dibuka, di mana anda boleh memilih tema (cerah, gelap, putih atas hitam, atau hitam atas putih), format (.svg atau .png), dan sama ada anda ingin menerapkan pembungkusan baris. Selepas anda memilih pilihan, klik Export.\n"

#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "3. Build your circuit with OpenQASM code {#3-build-your-circuit-with-openqasm-code}"
msgstr "3. Bina Circuit anda dengan kod OpenQASM {#3-build-your-circuit-with-openqasm-code}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<Admonition type=\"note\">\n"
"IBM Quantum Composer currently supports OpenQASM 2.0.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"
msgstr ""
"<Admonition type=\"note\">\n"
"IBM Quantum Composer kini menyokong OpenQASM 2.0.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"

#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, no-wrap
msgid "To open the code editor, click View → Panels → Code Editor.\n"
msgstr "Untuk membuka editor kod, klik View → Panels → Code Editor.\n"

#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, no-wrap
msgid "See the [Composer operations glossary](#composer-operations-glossary) for OpenQASM references to gates and other operations.\n"
msgstr "Lihat [Glosari operasi Composer](#composer-operations-glossary) untuk rujukan OpenQASM kepada gate dan operasi lain.\n"

#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, no-wrap
msgid "You can define your own custom operations; see [Create a custom operation in OpenQASM](#create-a-custom-operation-in-openqasm).\n"
msgstr "Anda boleh menakrifkan operasi tersuai anda sendiri; lihat [Cipta operasi tersuai dalam OpenQASM](#create-a-custom-operation-in-openqasm).\n"

#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, no-wrap
msgid "For more information on using the OpenQASM language, including sample lines of code, see the [Introduction to OpenQASM](/guides/introduction-to-qasm) guide, or read the original research paper, [Open Quantum Assembly Language](https://arxiv.org/abs/1707.03429). The [table](https://arxiv.org/pdf/1707.03429.pdf#page=9) of OpenQASM language statements from the paper is reproduced below. The OpenQASM grammar can be found in [Appendix A](https://arxiv.org/pdf/1707.03429.pdf#page=21) of the paper.\n"
msgstr "Untuk maklumat lanjut tentang penggunaan bahasa OpenQASM, termasuk baris kod contoh, lihat panduan [Pengenalan kepada OpenQASM](/guides/introduction-to-qasm), atau baca kertas penyelidikan asal, [Open Quantum Assembly Language](https://arxiv.org/abs/1707.03429). [Jadual](https://arxiv.org/pdf/1707.03429.pdf#page=9) pernyataan bahasa OpenQASM daripada kertas itu dihasilkan semula di bawah. Tatabahasa OpenQASM boleh didapati dalam [Lampiran A](https://arxiv.org/pdf/1707.03429.pdf#page=21) kertas tersebut.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<p></p>\n"
"<table width=\"100%\">\n"
"<thead>\n"
"<tr>\n"
"<th>Statement</th>\n"
"<th>Description</th>\n"
"<th>Example</th>\n"
"</tr>\n"
"</thead>\n"
"<tbody><tr>\n"
"<td><code>OPENQASM 2.0;</code></td>\n"
"<td>Denotes a file in OpenQASM format (see [a])</td>\n"
"<td><code>OPENQASM 2.0;</code></td>\n"
"</tr>\n"
"<tr>\n"
"<td><code>qreg name[size];</code></td>\n"
"<td>Declare a named register of qubits</td>\n"
"<td><code>qreg q[5];</code></td>\n"
"</tr>\n"
"<tr>\n"
"<td><code>creg name[size];</code></td>\n"
"<td>Declare a named register of bits</td>\n"
"<td><code>creg c[5];</code></td>\n"
"</tr>\n"
"<tr>\n"
"<td><code>include “filename”;</code></td>\n"
"<td>Open and parse another source file</td>\n"
"<td><code>include “qelib1.inc”;</code></td>\n"
"</tr>\n"
"<tr>\n"
"<td><code>gate name(params) qargs</code></td>\n"
"<td>Declare a unitary gate</td>\n"
"<td>(see text of paper)</td>\n"
"</tr>\n"
"<tr>\n"
"<td><code>opaque name(params) qargs;</code></td>\n"
"<td>Declare an opaque gate</td>\n"
"<td>(see text of paper)</td>\n"
"</tr>\n"
"<tr>\n"
"<td><code>// comment text</code></td>\n"
"<td>Comment a line of text</td>\n"
"<td><code>// oops!</code></td>\n"
"</tr>\n"
"<tr>\n"
"<td><code>U(theta,phi,lambda) qubit|qreg;</code></td>\n"
"<td>Apply built-in single-qubit gate(s) (see [b])</td>\n"
"<td><code>U(pi/2,2\\*pi/3,0) q[0];</code></td>\n"
"</tr>\n"
"<tr>\n"
"<td><code>CX qubit|qreg,qubit|qreg;</code></td>\n"
"<td>Apply built-in CNOT gate(s)</td>\n"
"<td><code>CX q[0],q[1];</code></td>\n"
"</tr>\n"
"<tr>\n"
"<td><code>measure qubit|qreg -&gt; bit|creg;</code></td>\n"
"<td>Make measurement(s) in $Z$ basis</td>\n"
"<td><code>measure q -&gt; c;</code></td>\n"
"</tr>\n"
"<tr>\n"
"<td><code>reset qubit|qreg;</code></td>\n"
"<td>Prepare qubit(s) in $\\vert 0\\rangle$</td>\n"
"<td><code>reset q[0];</code></td>\n"
"</tr>\n"
"<tr>\n"
"<td><code>gatename(params) qargs;</code></td>\n"
"<td>Apply a user-defined unitary gate</td>\n"
"<td><code>crz(pi/2) q[1],q[0];</code></td>\n"
"</tr>\n"
"<tr>\n"
"<td><code>if(creg==int) qop;</code></td>\n"
"<td>Conditionally apply quantum operation</td>\n"
"<td><code>if(c==5) CX q[0],q[1];</code></td>\n"
"</tr>\n"
"<tr>\n"
"<td><code>barrier qargs;</code></td>\n"
"<td>Prevent transformations across this source line</td>\n"
"<td><code>barrier q[0],q[1];</code></td>\n"
"</tr>\n"
"</tbody></table>\n"
msgstr ""
"<p></p>\n"
"<table width=\"100%\">\n"
"<thead>\n"
"<tr>\n"
"<th>Pernyataan</th>\n"
"<th>Penerangan</th>\n"
"<th>Contoh</th>\n"
"</tr>\n"
"</thead>\n"
"<tbody><tr>\n"
"<td><code>OPENQASM 2.0;</code></td>\n"
"<td>Menandakan fail dalam format OpenQASM (lihat [a])</td>\n"
"<td><code>OPENQASM 2.0;</code></td>\n"
"</tr>\n"
"<tr>\n"
"<td><code>qreg name[size];</code></td>\n"
"<td>Isytihar daftar qubit bernama</td>\n"
"<td><code>qreg q[5];</code></td>\n"
"</tr>\n"
"<tr>\n"
"<td><code>creg name[size];</code></td>\n"
"<td>Isytihar daftar bit bernama</td>\n"
"<td><code>creg c[5];</code></td>\n"
"</tr>\n"
"<tr>\n"
"<td><code>include \"filename\";</code></td>\n"
"<td>Buka dan urai fail sumber lain</td>\n"
"<td><code>include \"qelib1.inc\";</code></td>\n"
"</tr>\n"
"<tr>\n"
"<td><code>gate name(params) qargs</code></td>\n"
"<td>Isytihar gate unitari</td>\n"
"<td>(lihat teks kertas)</td>\n"
"</tr>\n"
"<tr>\n"
"<td><code>opaque name(params) qargs;</code></td>\n"
"<td>Isytihar gate legap</td>\n"
"<td>(lihat teks kertas)</td>\n"
"</tr>\n"
"<tr>\n"
"<td><code>// comment text</code></td>\n"
"<td>Komen baris teks</td>\n"
"<td><code>// oops!</code></td>\n"
"</tr>\n"
"<tr>\n"
"<td><code>U(theta,phi,lambda) qubit|qreg;</code></td>\n"
"<td>Terapkan gate satu qubit terbina dalam (lihat [b])</td>\n"
"<td><code>U(pi/2,2\\*pi/3,0) q[0];</code></td>\n"
"</tr>\n"
"<tr>\n"
"<td><code>CX qubit|qreg,qubit|qreg;</code></td>\n"
"<td>Terapkan gate CNOT terbina dalam</td>\n"
"<td><code>CX q[0],q[1];</code></td>\n"
"</tr>\n"
"<tr>\n"
"<td><code>measure qubit|qreg -&gt; bit|creg;</code></td>\n"
"<td>Buat pengukuran dalam asas $Z$</td>\n"
"<td><code>measure q -&gt; c;</code></td>\n"
"</tr>\n"
"<tr>\n"
"<td><code>reset qubit|qreg;</code></td>\n"
"<td>Sediakan qubit dalam keadaan $\\vert 0\\rangle$</td>\n"
"<td><code>reset q[0];</code></td>\n"
"</tr>\n"
"<tr>\n"
"<td><code>gatename(params) qargs;</code></td>\n"
"<td>Terapkan gate unitari yang ditakrifkan pengguna</td>\n"
"<td><code>crz(pi/2) q[1],q[0];</code></td>\n"
"</tr>\n"
"<tr>\n"
"<td><code>if(creg==int) qop;</code></td>\n"
"<td>Terapkan operasi kuantum secara bersyarat</td>\n"
"<td><code>if(c==5) CX q[0],q[1];</code></td>\n"
"</tr>\n"
"<tr>\n"
"<td><code>barrier qargs;</code></td>\n"
"<td>Halang transformasi merentasi baris sumber ini</td>\n"
"<td><code>barrier q[0],q[1];</code></td>\n"
"</tr>\n"
"</tbody></table>\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "\\[a] This must appear as the first non-comment line of the file.\n"
msgstr "\\[a] Ini mesti muncul sebagai baris bukan ulasan pertama fail.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "\\[b] The parameters theta, phi, and lambda are given by *parameter expressions*; for more information, see [page 5 of the paper](https://arxiv.org/abs/1707.03429#page=5) and [Appendix A](https://arxiv.org/pdf/1707.03429.pdf#page=21).\n"
msgstr "\\[b] Parameter theta, phi, dan lambda diberikan oleh *ungkapan parameter*; untuk maklumat lanjut, lihat [halaman 5 kertas](https://arxiv.org/abs/1707.03429#page=5) dan [Lampiran A](https://arxiv.org/pdf/1707.03429.pdf#page=21).\n"

#. type: Title ####
#, no-wrap
msgid "Create a custom operation in OpenQASM {#create-a-custom-operation-in-openqasm}"
msgstr "Cipta operasi tersuai dalam OpenQASM {#create-a-custom-operation-in-openqasm}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "You can define new unitary operations in the code editor (see the figure below for an example). The operations are applied using the statement `name(params) qargs;` just like the built-in operations. The parentheses are optional if there are no parameters.\n"
msgstr "Anda boleh menakrifkan operasi unitari baharu dalam editor kod (lihat rajah di bawah sebagai contoh). Operasi diterapkan menggunakan pernyataan `name(params) qargs;` sama seperti operasi terbina dalam. Tanda kurung adalah pilihan jika tiada parameter.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "To define a custom operation, enter it in the OpenQASM code editor using this format: `gatename(params) qargs;`. If you click **+Add** in the operations list, you will be prompted to enter a name for your custom operation, which you can then build in the code editor.\n"
msgstr "Untuk menakrifkan operasi tersuai, masukkannya dalam editor kod OpenQASM menggunakan format ini: `gatename(params) qargs;`. Jika anda klik **+Add** dalam senarai operasi, anda akan diminta untuk memasukkan nama bagi operasi tersuai anda, yang kemudiannya boleh anda bina dalam editor kod.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Once you have defined your custom operation, drag it onto the graphical editor and use the edit icon to fine-tune the parameters.\n"
msgstr "Setelah anda menakrifkan operasi tersuai, seret operasi tersebut ke editor grafik dan gunakan ikon edit untuk memperhalusi parameter.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"| Example of a custom operation | |\n"
"| --- | --- |\n"
"| The gates to be included in the custom operation: | ![Gates in the custom operation](/docs/images/guides/composer/763d3b42-4b6e-4409-817f-7d15abae2d76.avif)|\n"
"| The code for the new operation: | ![Customized new operation](/docs/images/guides/composer/db5856ca-751c-4f12-9f25-6060b9003687.avif) | \n"
"| The new operation in the graphical editor: | ![New operation](/docs/images/guides/composer/d7fb8ec5-5eae-4ad4-9972-1e3665b39b7f.avif) |\n"
msgstr ""
"| Contoh operasi tersuai | |\n"
"| --- | --- |\n"
"| gate yang hendak disertakan dalam operasi tersuai: | ![gate dalam operasi tersuai](/docs/images/guides/composer/763d3b42-4b6e-4409-817f-7d15abae2d76.avif)|\n"
"| Kod untuk operasi baharu: | ![Operasi baharu yang disesuaikan](/docs/images/guides/composer/db5856ca-751c-4f12-9f25-6060b9003687.avif) |\n"
"| Operasi baharu dalam editor grafik: | ![Operasi baharu](/docs/images/guides/composer/d7fb8ec5-5eae-4ad4-9972-1e3665b39b7f.avif) |\n"

#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "4. Inspect your circuit, step-by-step {#4-inspect-your-circuit-step-by-step}"
msgstr "4. Semak Circuit anda, langkah demi langkah {#4-inspect-your-circuit-step-by-step}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Inspect mode de-mystifies the inner workings of the circuits you create. It steps through a simulation of your circuit, one layer at a time, so that you can see the state of the qubits as the computation evolves.\n"
msgstr "Mod semak menyingkap cara kerja dalaman Circuit yang anda cipta. Ia melangkah melalui simulasi Circuit anda, satu lapisan pada satu masa, supaya anda dapat melihat keadaan qubit semasa pengiraan berkembang.\n"

#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, no-wrap
msgid "In the **View** menu, select the panels for the visualizations that you want to use.\n"
msgstr "Dalam menu **View**, pilih panel untuk gambaran visual yang anda ingin gunakan.\n"

#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Click the **Inspect** toggle in the toolbar. Note that once Inspect mode is toggled on, you cannot add any more operations until it is turned off again.\n"
msgstr "Klik togol **Inspect** dalam bar alat. Perhatikan bahawa setelah mod Inspect dihidupkan, anda tidak boleh menambah sebarang operasi lagi sehingga ia dimatikan semula.\n"

#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, no-wrap
msgid "If you built your circuit with the Freeform alignment turned on, note that Inspect mode automatically turns on the Left alignment.\n"
msgstr "Jika anda membina Circuit anda dengan penjajaran Freeform dihidupkan, perhatikan bahawa mod Inspect secara automatik menghidupkan penjajaran Left.\n"

#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, no-wrap
msgid "To move step-by-step through visualizations of your circuit’s components, use the forward and rewind buttons.\n"
msgstr "Untuk melangkah maju dan mundur melalui gambaran visual komponen Circuit anda, gunakan butang maju dan undur.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "![Controls to step forward and backward, and to jump to a circuit's beginning or end.](/docs/images/guides/composer/5f2dfb7c-a244-405c-8950-f422a4408fcf.avif \"Inspect mode controls, in order: jump to the beginning of a circuit, step backward, play from one break point to the next, step forward, jump to the end of a circuit.\")\n"
msgstr "![Kawalan untuk melangkah maju dan mundur, serta untuk melompat ke permulaan atau penghujung Circuit.](/docs/images/guides/composer/5f2dfb7c-a244-405c-8950-f422a4408fcf.avif \"Kawalan mod semak, mengikut urutan: lompat ke permulaan Circuit, langkah mundur, main dari satu titik henti ke seterusnya, langkah maju, lompat ke penghujung Circuit.\")\n"

#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, no-wrap
msgid "To inspect only some operations, click the operations you want to be inspected, and a colored overlay appears over each that indicates they will be included when you run in Inspect mode. To unselect an operation, click on it again, and the overlay disappears.\n"
msgstr "Untuk menyemak hanya sebahagian operasi, klik operasi yang anda ingin semak, dan hamparan berwarna muncul pada setiap operasi yang menunjukkan ia akan disertakan apabila anda menjalankan mod Inspect. Untuk menyahpilih operasi, klik semula, dan hamparan tersebut hilang.\n"

#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, no-wrap
msgid "To learn more about interpreting visualizations, see the [Visualizations](#visualizations) topic.\n"
msgstr "Untuk mengetahui lebih lanjut tentang mentafsirkan gambaran visual, lihat topik [Gambaran visual](#visualizations).\n"

#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, no-wrap
msgid "To exit Inspect mode and return to editing your circuit, click the Inspect toggle in the toolbar.\n"
msgstr "Untuk keluar daripada mod Inspect dan kembali mengedit Circuit, klik togol Inspect dalam bar alat.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<Admonition type=\"note\" title=\"Randomness in the simulator\">\n"
"The simulator creates randomness by generating results based on a *seed*. The seed is the initial value introduced into the algorithm that generates pseudorandom numbers. You can see the seed number by selecting \"Visualizations seed\" from the Edit menu. You can also set the seed yourself by changing the value in the box.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"
msgstr ""
"<Admonition type=\"note\" title=\"Kerawakan dalam simulator\">\n"
"Simulator mencipta kerawakan dengan menjana keputusan berdasarkan *benih*. Benih ialah nilai awal yang dimasukkan ke dalam algoritma yang menjana nombor pseudorawak. Anda boleh melihat nombor benih dengan memilih \"Visualizations seed\" daripada menu Edit. Anda juga boleh menetapkan benih sendiri dengan mengubah nilai dalam kotak tersebut.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"

#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Run circuits and view results {#run-circuits-and-view-results}"
msgstr "Jalankan litar dan lihat keputusan {#run-circuits-and-view-results}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Follow the steps below to run quantum circuits on QPUs and view the results.\n"
msgstr "Ikut langkah-langkah di bawah untuk menjalankan Circuit quantum pada QPU dan melihat keputusannya.\n"

#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Choose your job settings {#choose-your-job-settings}"
msgstr "Pilih tetapan kerja anda {#choose-your-job-settings}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Click **Run circuit** in the upper right corner. In the window that opens, select an available QPU. You can also choose an instance, which is associated with a plan (such as the Open, Flex, or Premium Plans). The instance you choose affects which QPUs are available to you. Click the \"View details\" link in the table of QPUs to see more information on each QPU.\n"
msgstr "Klik **Run circuit** di penjuru kanan atas. Dalam tetingkap yang terbuka, pilih QPU yang tersedia. Anda juga boleh memilih instance, yang dikaitkan dengan pelan tertentu (seperti Pelan Open, Flex, atau Premium). Instance yang anda pilih mempengaruhi QPU mana yang tersedia untuk anda. Klik pautan \"View details\" dalam jadual QPU untuk melihat maklumat lanjut tentang setiap QPU.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Next, you can set the number of shots (executions) of your circuit that the backend will perform.\n"
msgstr "Seterusnya, anda boleh tetapkan bilangan shot (pelaksanaan) litar anda yang akan dilakukan oleh Backend.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "You can optionally name the job and add tags in this panel as well. This will not change the name of the circuit. A pre-populated \"Composer\" tag makes it easier to filter your Workloads table by Composer jobs. You can remove this tag.\n"
msgstr "Anda juga boleh menamakan kerja dan menambah tag dalam panel ini. Ini tidak akan mengubah nama litar. Tag \"Composer\" yang telah dipra-isi memudahkan anda menapis jadual Workloads mengikut kerja Composer. Anda boleh membuang tag ini.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "![Window displaying job options.](/docs/images/guides/composer/composer-run.svg)\n"
msgstr "![Tetingkap yang menunjukkan pilihan kerja.](/docs/images/guides/composer/composer-run.svg)\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<Admonition type=\"note\">\n"
"When you run a circuit, it is automatically sent to the least-busy QPU, unless you specify a QPU in the Run settings. If you run the same circuit again, the QPU selection window will default to your previous choice.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"
msgstr ""
"<Admonition type=\"note\">\n"
"Apabila anda menjalankan litar, ia dihantar secara automatik ke QPU yang paling kurang sibuk, melainkan anda menyatakan QPU dalam tetapan Run. Jika anda menjalankan litar yang sama sekali lagi, tetingkap pemilihan QPU akan menggunakan pilihan anda yang terdahulu sebagai lalai.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"

#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Click \"Run on (QPU name)\" {#click-run-on-qpu-name}"
msgstr "Klik \"Run on (nama QPU)\" {#click-run-on-qpu-name}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "You can view the job’s progress by clicking the \"View jobs\" button in the top-right corner, which will open the Workloads page in IBM Quantum Platform.\n"
msgstr "Anda boleh melihat kemajuan kerja dengan mengklik butang \"View jobs\" di penjuru kanan atas, yang akan membuka halaman Workloads dalam IBM Quantum Platform.\n"

#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "View results {#view-results}"
msgstr "Lihat keputusan {#view-results}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Once your job completes, the details are updated in the Workloads table in IBM Quantum Platform.\n"
msgstr "Setelah kerja anda selesai, butiran dikemas kini dalam jadual Workloads di IBM Quantum Platform.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The Jobs results page displays run details, diagrams of the original and the transpiled circuit, a histogram of the results, and OpenQASM and Qiskit tabs to view both original and transpiled circuits in OpenQASM or Qiskit.\n"
msgstr "Halaman keputusan Jobs memaparkan butiran pelarian, gambar rajah litar asal dan litar yang telah ditranspil, histogram keputusan, serta tab OpenQASM dan Qiskit untuk melihat kedua-dua litar asal dan yang telah ditranspil dalam OpenQASM atau Qiskit.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "You can download the circuits and the histogram by clicking the menu in the upper right corner of each diagram, then selecting a format for the download (PNG, PDF, or SVG; additionally, you can export the histogram as a CSV file). You can open the OpenQASM circuits directly in Composer.\n"
msgstr "Anda boleh memuat turun litar dan histogram dengan mengklik menu di penjuru kanan atas setiap gambar rajah, kemudian memilih format muat turun (PNG, PDF, atau SVG; selain itu, anda boleh mengeksport histogram sebagai fail CSV). Anda boleh membuka litar OpenQASM terus dalam Composer.\n"

#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Visualizations {#visualizations}"
msgstr "Visualisasi {#visualizations}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The live visualizations in IBM Quantum Composer show you different views of how quantum circuits affect the state of a collection of qubits. Each type of live visualization is explained in detail below.\n"
msgstr "Visualisasi langsung dalam IBM Quantum Composer menunjukkan pandangan berbeza tentang bagaimana Circuit quantum mempengaruhi keadaan koleksi qubit. Setiap jenis visualisasi langsung dijelaskan secara terperinci di bawah.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<Admonition type=\"note\" title=\"Randomness in the simulator\">\n"
"The live visualizations come from a single-shot statevector simulator, which is different from the QPU specified in the Run settings, which can have multiple shots. The simulator creates randomness by generating results based on a *seed*. The seed is the initial value introduced into the algorithm that generates pseudorandom numbers. You can see the seed number by selecting \"Visualizations seed\" from the Edit menu. You can also set the seed yourself by changing the value in the box.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"
msgstr ""
"<Admonition type=\"note\" title=\"Rawak dalam simulator\">\n"
"Visualisasi langsung datang daripada simulator statevector satu shot, yang berbeza daripada QPU yang dinyatakan dalam tetapan Run, yang boleh mempunyai berbilang shot. Simulator mencipta rawak dengan menjana keputusan berdasarkan *seed*. Seed ialah nilai awal yang diperkenalkan ke dalam algoritma yang menjana nombor pseudorawak. Anda boleh melihat nombor seed dengan memilih \"Visualizations seed\" daripada menu Edit. Anda juga boleh menetapkan seed sendiri dengan mengubah nilai dalam kotak.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"

#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "View visualizations {#view-visualizations}"
msgstr "Lihat visualisasi {#view-visualizations}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The live visualizations are shown in windows at the bottom of the Composer workspace (except the phase disk, which appears at the end of each qubit wire). You can choose any combination of statevector, probabilities, and q-sphere visualizations to appear at the bottom of the workspace. Select or unselect visualizations in the **View** menu.\n"
msgstr "Visualisasi langsung ditunjukkan dalam tetingkap di bahagian bawah ruang kerja Composer (kecuali cakera fasa, yang muncul di hujung setiap wayar qubit). Anda boleh memilih mana-mana kombinasi visualisasi statevector, kebarangkalian, dan q-sphere untuk muncul di bahagian bawah ruang kerja. Pilih atau nyahpilih visualisasi dalam menu **View**.\n"

#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Download visualizations {#download-visualizations}"
msgstr "Muat turun visualisasi {#download-visualizations}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Download one of the visualizations at the bottom of the Composer workspace by clicking the \"More options\" menu in the visualization window. You can download visualizations as an SVG, a PNG, or a CSV of the underlying data. You can also download the visualization images of the measurement probabilities and statevector histograms as a PDF.\n"
msgstr "Muat turun salah satu visualisasi di bahagian bawah ruang kerja Composer dengan mengklik menu \"More options\" dalam tetingkap visualisasi. Anda boleh memuat turun visualisasi sebagai SVG, PNG, atau CSV data yang mendasarinya. Anda juga boleh memuat turun imej visualisasi kebarangkalian pengukuran dan histogram statevector sebagai PDF.\n"

#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Phase disk {#phase-disk}"
msgstr "Cakera fasa {#phase-disk}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "A single-qubit state can be represented as\n"
msgstr "Keadaan qubit tunggal boleh diwakilkan sebagai\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{split}\\vert\\psi\\rangle = \\sqrt{1-p}\\vert0\\rangle + e^{j\\varphi} \\sqrt{p} \\vert1\\rangle,\\end{split}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{split}\\vert\\psi\\rangle = \\sqrt{1-p}\\vert0\\rangle + e^{j\\varphi} \\sqrt{p} \\vert1\\rangle,\\end{split}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "where $p$ is the probability that the qubit is in the $|1\\rangle$ state, and $\\varphi$ is the quantum phase. $p$ is strongly analogous to a classical probabilistic bit. For $p=0$, the qubit is in the $|0\\rangle$ state, for $p=1$ the qubit is in the $|1\\rangle$ state, and for $p=1/2$ the qubit is a 50/50 mixture. We call this a superposition as, unlike classical bits, this mixture can have a quantum phase. The phase disk visualizes this state.\n"
msgstr "di mana $p$ ialah kebarangkalian qubit berada dalam keadaan $|1\\rangle$, dan $\\varphi$ ialah fasa quantum. $p$ sangat analog dengan bit kebarangkalian klasik. Untuk $p=0$, qubit berada dalam keadaan $|0\\rangle$, untuk $p=1$ qubit berada dalam keadaan $|1\\rangle$, dan untuk $p=1/2$ qubit adalah campuran 50/50. Kita menyebut ini sebagai superposisi kerana, tidak seperti bit klasik, campuran ini boleh mempunyai fasa quantum. Cakera fasa menggambarkan keadaan ini.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The phase disk at the terminus of each qubit in IBM Quantum Composer gives the local state of each qubit at the end of the computation. The components of the phase disk are described below.\n"
msgstr "Cakera fasa di penghujung setiap qubit dalam IBM Quantum Composer memberikan keadaan setempat setiap qubit pada penghujung pengiraan. Komponen cakera fasa diterangkan di bawah.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Probability the qubit is in the** $|1\\rangle$ **state**\n"
msgstr "**Kebarangkalian qubit berada dalam keadaan** $|1\\rangle$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The probability that the qubit is in the $|1\\rangle$ state is represented by the blue disk fill.\n"
msgstr "Kebarangkalian qubit berada dalam keadaan $|1\\rangle$ diwakili oleh isian cakera biru.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "![probability the qubit is in the 1 state](/docs/images/guides/composer/3e4140c6-9da0-46b0-85e4-a1509078d3e9.avif)\n"
msgstr "![kebarangkalian qubit berada dalam keadaan 1](/docs/images/guides/composer/3e4140c6-9da0-46b0-85e4-a1509078d3e9.avif)\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Quantum phase**\n"
msgstr "**Fasa quantum**\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The quantum phase of the qubit state is given by the line that extends from the center of the diagram to the edge of the gray disk (which rotates counterclockwise around the center point).\n"
msgstr "Fasa quantum keadaan qubit diberikan oleh garisan yang memanjang dari pusat gambar rajah ke tepi cakera kelabu (yang berputar lawan arah jam di sekitar titik tengah).\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "![phase of the local qubit state](/docs/images/guides/composer/7f047fde-c19e-46db-b596-be5da55e697e.avif)\n"
msgstr "![fasa keadaan qubit setempat](/docs/images/guides/composer/7f047fde-c19e-46db-b596-be5da55e697e.avif)\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Example: phase disks for two different qubits**\n"
msgstr "**Contoh: cakera fasa untuk dua qubit berbeza**\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "![phase disk examples](/docs/images/guides/composer/0207fba8-8b4b-4611-9638-6cbe169e10c4.avif)\n"
msgstr "![contoh cakera fasa](/docs/images/guides/composer/0207fba8-8b4b-4611-9638-6cbe169e10c4.avif)\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Two examples of the phase disk visualization. The first example is a $|1\\rangle$ state and the second shows the $(|0\\rangle-|1\\rangle)/\\sqrt{2}$ state with a nonzero relative phase.\n"
msgstr "Dua contoh visualisasi cakera fasa. Contoh pertama ialah keadaan $|1\\rangle$ dan yang kedua menunjukkan keadaan $(|0\\rangle-|1\\rangle)/\\sqrt{2}$ dengan fasa relatif yang bukan sifar.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Connection to the Bloch sphere**\n"
msgstr "**Hubungan dengan sfera Bloch**\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The phase disk, which contains all the information in the Bloch sphere, is a two-dimensional representation of a qubit. To convert to the Bloch sphere representation: $x=2\\sqrt{p(1-p)}\\mathrm{Re}[e^{j\\varphi} ]$, $y=2\\sqrt{p(1-p)}\\mathrm{Im}[e^{j\\varphi} ]$, and $z=1-2p$.\n"
msgstr "Cakera fasa, yang mengandungi semua maklumat dalam sfera Bloch, ialah representasi dua dimensi bagi sebuah qubit. Untuk menukar ke representasi sfera Bloch: $x=2\\sqrt{p(1-p)}\\mathrm{Re}[e^{j\\varphi} ]$, $y=2\\sqrt{p(1-p)}\\mathrm{Im}[e^{j\\varphi} ]$, dan $z=1-2p$.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "**N-qubit states: maximum 15 qubits**\n"
msgstr "**Keadaan N-Qubit: maksimum 15 qubit**\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "An N-qubit quantum state takes the form\n"
msgstr "Keadaan quantum N-Qubit mengambil bentuk\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{split}\\vert\\psi\\rangle = \\sqrt{1-p}\\vert0...0\\rangle + \\sum_{k=1}^{2^N-1}e^{j\\varphi_k} \\sqrt{p_k} \\vert k\\rangle,\\end{split}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{split}\\vert\\psi\\rangle = \\sqrt{1-p}\\vert0...0\\rangle + \\sum_{k=1}^{2^N-1}e^{j\\varphi_k} \\sqrt{p_k} \\vert k\\rangle,\\end{split}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "where $p_k$ is the probability that the qubits are in the state $|k\\rangle$ with quantum phase $\\varphi_k$ with respect to the $|0...0\\rangle$ state. $p=\\sum_{k\\neq0}p_k$ is the probability that the qubits are not in the ground state $|0...0\\rangle$. Here it is simple to see that for an N-qubit quantum state there are $2^N-1$ probabilities and $2^N-1$ phases. The phase disk fails to represent this state, as N-qubit phase disks would only contain $N$ probabilities and $N$ phases; this is because most states are entangled and are not separable into independent single-qubit quantum states. To represent that full information is not contained in this visualization, we introduce the reduced purity as a component in the phase disk.\n"
msgstr "di mana $p_k$ ialah kebarangkalian qubit berada dalam keadaan $|k\\rangle$ dengan fasa quantum $\\varphi_k$ terhadap keadaan $|0...0\\rangle$. $p=\\sum_{k\\neq0}p_k$ ialah kebarangkalian bahawa qubit tidak berada dalam keadaan asas $|0...0\\rangle$. Di sini mudah untuk dilihat bahawa bagi keadaan quantum N-Qubit terdapat $2^N-1$ kebarangkalian dan $2^N-1$ fasa. Cakera fasa gagal mewakili keadaan ini, kerana cakera fasa N-Qubit hanya mengandungi $N$ kebarangkalian dan $N$ fasa; ini kerana kebanyakan keadaan adalah terjalin dan tidak boleh dipisahkan kepada keadaan quantum qubit tunggal yang bebas. Untuk mewakili bahawa maklumat penuh tidak terkandung dalam visualisasi ini, kami memperkenalkan kemurnian terkurang sebagai komponen dalam cakera fasa.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Reduced purity of the qubit state**\n"
msgstr "**Kemurnian terkurang keadaan qubit**\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The radius of the black ring on the phase disk represents the reduced purity of the qubit state, which for qubit $j$ in an $N$-qubit state $|\\psi\\rangle$ is given by $\\mathrm{Tr}\\left[\\mathrm{Tr}_{i\\neq j}[\\left|\\psi\\rangle\\langle\\psi\\right|\\right]^{2}]$. The reduced purity for a single qubit is in the range $[0.5, 1]$; a value of one indicates that the qubit is not entangled with any other party. In contrast, a reduced purity of $0.5$ shows that the qubit is left in the completely mixed state, and has some level of entanglement over the remaining $N-1$ qubits, and possibly even the environment.\n"
msgstr "Jejari cincin hitam pada cakera fasa mewakili kemurnian terkurang keadaan qubit, yang untuk qubit $j$ dalam keadaan $N$-Qubit $|\\psi\\rangle$ diberikan oleh $\\mathrm{Tr}\\left[\\mathrm{Tr}_{i\\neq j}[\\left|\\psi\\rangle\\langle\\psi\\right|\\right]^{2}]$. Kemurnian terkurang untuk qubit tunggal berada dalam julat $[0.5, 1]$; nilai satu menunjukkan bahawa qubit tidak terjalin dengan mana-mana pihak lain. Sebaliknya, kemurnian terkurang sebesar $0.5$ menunjukkan bahawa qubit berada dalam keadaan campuran sepenuhnya, dan mempunyai tahap keterjalinan tertentu ke atas baki $N-1$ qubit, dan mungkin juga persekitaran.\n"

#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Probabilities view {#probabilities-view}"
msgstr "Paparan kebarangkalian {#probabilities-view}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "**8-qubit limit**\n"
msgstr "**Had 8 qubit**\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "This view visualizes the probabilities of the quantum state as a bar graph. The horizontal axis labels the computational basis states. The vertical axis measures the probabilities in terms of percentages. In this view the quantum phases are not represented, and is therefore an incomplete representation. However, it is useful for predicting the outcomes if each qubit is measured and the value stored in its own classical bit.\n"
msgstr "Paparan ini menggambarkan kebarangkalian keadaan quantum sebagai graf bar. Paksi mendatar melabelkan keadaan asas pengiraan. Paksi menegak mengukur kebarangkalian dalam peratusan. Dalam paparan ini fasa quantum tidak diwakili, dan oleh itu merupakan representasi yang tidak lengkap. Walau bagaimanapun, ia berguna untuk meramalkan hasil jika setiap qubit diukur dan nilainya disimpan dalam bit klasik masing-masing.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Consider the following quantum circuit and its probabilities view:\n"
msgstr "Pertimbangkan litar quantum berikut dan paparan kebarangkaliannya:\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "![a quantum circuit](/docs/images/guides/composer/2H-circuit.svg \"A circuit consisting of a column of Hadamards that creates an equal superposition of the computational basis states, followed by a two-qubit controlled-Z (CZ) gate.\")\n"
msgstr "![litar quantum](/docs/images/guides/composer/2H-circuit.svg \"Litar yang terdiri daripada lajur Hadamard yang mencipta superposisi sama rata bagi keadaan asas pengiraan, diikuti oleh gate controlled-Z (CZ) dua qubit.\")\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "![Probabilities view of the previous circuit](/docs/images/guides/composer/probabilities.svg \"Probabilities view of the previous circuit.\")\n"
msgstr "![Paparan kebarangkalian bagi litar sebelumnya](/docs/images/guides/composer/probabilities.svg \"Paparan kebarangkalian bagi litar sebelumnya.\")\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The circuit puts the two qubits into the state $|\\psi\\rangle = (|00\\rangle + |01\\rangle+ |10\\rangle-|11\\rangle) / 2$. The computational basis states are $|00\\rangle, |10\\rangle, |01\\rangle$, and $|11\\rangle$. The probabilities for each of the computational states is 1/4.\n"
msgstr "Litar meletakkan dua qubit ke dalam keadaan $|\\psi\\rangle = (|00\\rangle + |01\\rangle+ |10\\rangle-|11\\rangle) / 2.$ Keadaan asas pengiraan adalah $|00\\rangle, |10\\rangle, |01\\rangle,$ dan $|11\\rangle.$ Kebarangkalian untuk setiap keadaan pengiraan ialah 1/4.\n"

#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Q-sphere view {#q-sphere-view}"
msgstr "Paparan Q-sphere {#q-sphere-view}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "**5-qubit limit**\n"
msgstr "**Had 5 qubit**\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The q-sphere represents the state of a system of one or more qubits by associating each computational basis state with a point on the surface of a sphere. A node is visible at each point. Each node’s radius is proportional to the probability ($p_k$) of its basis state, whereas the node color indicates the quantum phase ($\\varphi_k$).\n"
msgstr "Q-sphere mewakili keadaan sistem satu atau lebih qubit dengan mengaitkan setiap keadaan asas pengiraan dengan titik di permukaan sfera. Nod kelihatan pada setiap titik. Jejari setiap nod adalah berkadar dengan kebarangkalian ($p_k$) keadaan asasnya, manakala warna nod menunjukkan fasa quantum ($\\varphi_k$).\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The nodes are laid out on the q-sphere so that the basis state with all zeros (e.g., $|000\\rangle)$ is at its north pole, and the basis state with all ones (e.g., $|111\\rangle$) is at its south pole. Basis states with the same number of zeros (or ones) lie on a shared latitude of the q-sphere (e.g., $|001\\rangle, |010\\rangle, |100\\rangle$). Beginning at the north pole of the q-sphere and progressing southward, each successive latitude has basis states with a greater number of ones; the latitude of a basis state is determined by its [Hamming distance](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hamming_distance) from the zero state. The q-sphere contains complete information about the quantum state in a compact representation.\n"
msgstr "Nod disusun pada q-sphere supaya keadaan asas dengan semua sifar (contohnya, $|000\\rangle)$ berada di kutub utaranya, dan keadaan asas dengan semua satu (contohnya, $|111\\rangle$) berada di kutub selatannya. Keadaan asas dengan bilangan sifar (atau satu) yang sama terletak pada latitud yang dikongsi bersama pada q-sphere (contohnya, $|001\\rangle, |010\\rangle, |100\\rangle$). Bermula di kutub utara q-sphere dan bergerak ke selatan, setiap latitud berturutan mempunyai keadaan asas dengan bilangan satu yang lebih banyak; latitud sesuatu keadaan asas ditentukan oleh [jarak Hamming](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hamming_distance)nya dari keadaan sifar. Q-sphere mengandungi maklumat lengkap tentang keadaan quantum dalam representasi yang padat.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Consider the following quantum circuit and its q-sphere, which represent the state the circuit creates:\n"
msgstr "Pertimbangkan litar quantum berikut dan q-sphere-nya, yang mewakili keadaan yang dicipta oleh litar:\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "![a quantum circuit](/docs/images/guides/composer/2H-circuit.svg)\n"
msgstr "![litar quantum](/docs/images/guides/composer/2H-circuit.svg)\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "![q-sphere view](/docs/images/guides/composer/q-sphere.avif)\n"
msgstr "![paparan q-sphere](/docs/images/guides/composer/q-sphere.avif)\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "You can select, hold, and drag to rotate the q-sphere. To return the q-sphere to its default orientation, select the **rewind-arrow button** to the top right of the q-sphere.\n"
msgstr "Anda boleh memilih, tahan, dan seret untuk memutar q-sphere. Untuk mengembalikan q-sphere ke orientasi lalainya, pilih **butang anak panah balik semula** di bahagian kanan atas q-sphere.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<Admonition type=\"note\" title=\"What is the difference between a Bloch sphere and a q-sphere?\">\n"
"It is important to highlight that the q-sphere is **not** the same as the Bloch sphere, even for a single qubit. Indeed, like the [phase disk](#phase-disk), the Bloch sphere gives a *local* view of the quantum state, where each qubit is viewed on its own. When trying to understand how registers of qubits (multi-qubit states) behave upon the application of quantum circuits, it is more insightful to take a *global* view and look at the quantum state in its entirety. The q-sphere provides a visual representation of the quantum state, and thus this *global* viewpoint. Therefore, when exploring quantum applications and algorithms on small numbers of qubits, the q-sphere should be the primary visualization method.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"
msgstr ""
"<Admonition type=\"note\" title=\"Apakah perbezaan antara sfera Bloch dan q-sphere?\">\n"
"Penting untuk ditegaskan bahawa q-sphere **bukan** sama dengan sfera Bloch, walaupun untuk qubit tunggal. Sesungguhnya, seperti [cakera fasa](#phase-disk), sfera Bloch memberikan pandangan *setempat* keadaan quantum, di mana setiap qubit dilihat secara tersendiri. Apabila cuba memahami bagaimana daftar qubit (keadaan berbilang qubit) berkelakuan semasa penerapan Circuit quantum, lebih bermanfaat untuk mengambil pandangan *global* dan melihat keadaan quantum secara keseluruhannya. Q-sphere menyediakan representasi visual keadaan quantum, dan oleh itu pandangan *global* ini. Oleh itu, apabila meneroka aplikasi dan algoritma quantum pada bilangan qubit yang kecil, q-sphere seharusnya menjadi kaedah visualisasi utama.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"

#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Statevector view {#statevector-view}"
msgstr "Paparan statevector {#statevector-view}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "**6-qubit limit**\n"
msgstr "**Had 6 qubit**\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "It is common to call $\\sqrt{p_k}e^{i\\varphi_k}$ the quantum amplitude. This view visualizes the quantum amplitudes as a bar graph. The horizontal axis labels the computational basis states. The vertical axis measures the magnitude of the amplitudes ($\\sqrt{p_k}$) associated with each computational basis state. The color of each bar represents the quantum phase (${\\varphi_k}$).\n"
msgstr "Adalah biasa untuk memanggil $\\sqrt{p_k}e^{i\\varphi_k}$ sebagai amplitud quantum. Paparan ini menggambarkan amplitud quantum sebagai graf bar. Paksi mendatar melabelkan keadaan asas pengiraan. Paksi menegak mengukur magnitud amplitud ($\\sqrt{p_k}$) yang dikaitkan dengan setiap keadaan asas pengiraan. Warna setiap bar mewakili fasa quantum (${\\varphi_k}$).\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Consider the following quantum circuit and its statevector view:\n"
msgstr "Pertimbangkan litar quantum berikut dan paparan statevector-nya:\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "![statevector view](/docs/images/guides/composer/state-vector.svg \"The statevector at the terminus of the above circuit. The color wheel maps phase angle to color. The output state is expressed as a list of complex numbers.\")\n"
msgstr "![paparan statevector](/docs/images/guides/composer/state-vector.svg \"Statevector di penghujung litar di atas. Roda warna memetakan sudut fasa kepada warna. Keadaan output dinyatakan sebagai senarai nombor kompleks.\")\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The circuit puts the two qubits into the state $|\\psi\\rangle = (|00\\rangle + |01\\rangle+ |10\\rangle-|11\\rangle) / 2$. The computational basis states are $|00\\rangle$, $|10\\rangle$, $|01\\rangle$, and $|11\\rangle$. The magnitudes of the amplitudes are $1/2$, and the quantum phases with respect to the ground state are $0$ for $|01\\rangle$ and $|10\\rangle$, and $\\pi$ for $|11\\rangle$.\n"
msgstr "Litar meletakkan dua qubit ke dalam keadaan $|\\psi\\rangle = (|00\\rangle + |01\\rangle+ |10\\rangle-|11\\rangle) / 2$. Keadaan asas pengiraan adalah $|00\\rangle$, $|10\\rangle$, $|01\\rangle$, dan $|11\\rangle$. Magnitud amplitud ialah $1/2$, dan fasa quantum terhadap keadaan asas ialah $0$ untuk $|01\\rangle$ dan $|10\\rangle$, dan $\\pi$ untuk $|11\\rangle$.\n"

#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Composer operations glossary {#composer-operations-glossary}"
msgstr "Glosari operasi Composer {#composer-operations-glossary}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "This page is a reference that defines the various classical and quantum operations you can use to manipulate qubits in a quantum circuit. Quantum operations include quantum gates, such as the Hadamard gate, as well as operations that are not quantum gates, such as the measurement operation.\n"
msgstr "Halaman ini ialah rujukan yang mentakrifkan pelbagai operasi klasik dan quantum yang boleh anda gunakan untuk memanipulasi qubit dalam Circuit quantum. Operasi quantum termasuk gate quantum, seperti gate Hadamard, serta operasi yang bukan gate quantum, seperti operasi pengukuran.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Each entry below provides details and the OpenQASM reference for each operation. See the topic on [Build your circuit with OpenQASM code](#3-build-your-circuit-with-openqasm-code) for more information.\n"
msgstr "Setiap entri di bawah menyediakan butiran dan rujukan OpenQASM untuk setiap operasi. Lihat topik tentang [Bina litar anda dengan kod OpenQASM](#3-build-your-circuit-with-openqasm-code) untuk maklumat lanjut.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The q-sphere image in each gate entry below shows the state after the gate operates on the initial equal superposition state $\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2^{n}}}\\sum_{i=0}^{2^{n}-1}|i\\rangle$, where $n$ is the number of qubits needed to support the gate. See the [q-sphere](#q-sphere-view) topic for more information on this visualization.\n"
msgstr "Imej q-sphere dalam setiap entri gate di bawah menunjukkan keadaan selepas gate beroperasi pada keadaan superposisi sama rata awal $\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2^{n}}}\\sum_{i=0}^{2^{n}-1}|i\\rangle$, di mana $n$ ialah bilangan qubit yang diperlukan untuk menyokong gate. Lihat topik [q-sphere](#q-sphere-view) untuk maklumat lanjut tentang visualisasi ini.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "You can define a custom operation to use in IBM Quantum Composer. For instructions, see the [Create a custom operation in OpenQASM](#create-a-custom-operation-in-openqasm) topic.\n"
msgstr "Anda boleh menentukan operasi tersuai untuk digunakan dalam IBM Quantum Composer. Untuk arahan, lihat topik [Cipta operasi tersuai dalam OpenQASM](#create-a-custom-operation-in-openqasm).\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<Admonition type=\"note\" title=\"Gate colors\">\n"
"The gate colors are slightly different in the light and dark themes. The colors from the light theme are shown here.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"
msgstr ""
"<Admonition type=\"note\" title=\"Warna gate\">\n"
"Warna gate sedikit berbeza dalam tema cerah dan gelap. Warna daripada tema cerah ditunjukkan di sini.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Click a quantum operation below to view its definition.\n"
msgstr "Klik operasi quantum di bawah untuk melihat definisinya.\n"

#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Classical gates {#classical-gates}"
msgstr "gate klasik {#classical-gates}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "**NOT Gate**\n"
msgstr "**gate NOT**\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The NOT gate, also known as the Pauli X gate, flips the $\\left|0\\right\\rangle$ state to $\\left|1\\right\\rangle$, and vice versa. The NOT gate is equivalent to RX for the angle $\\pi$ or to ‘HZH’.\n"
msgstr "Gate NOT, juga dikenali sebagai gate Pauli X, membalikkan keadaan $\\left|0\\right\\rangle$ kepada $\\left|1\\right\\rangle$, dan sebaliknya. Gate NOT bersamaan dengan RX untuk sudut $\\pi$ atau dengan 'HZH'.\n"

