#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Phase gate**\n"
msgstr "**gate fasa**\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The Phase gate (previously called the U1 gate) applies a phase of $e^{i\\theta}$ to the $\\left|1\\right\\rangle$ state. For certain values of $\\theta$, it is equivalent to other gates. For example, P($\\pi$)=Z, P($\\pi$/$2$)=S, and P($\\pi/4$)=T. Up to a global phase of $e^{i\\theta/2}$, it is equivalent to RZ($\\theta$).\n"
msgstr "Gate Phase (sebelum ini dipanggil gate U1) menggunakan fasa $e^{i\\theta}$ kepada keadaan $\\left|1\\right\\rangle$. Untuk nilai-nilai $\\theta$ tertentu, ia bersamaan dengan gate lain. Contohnya, P($\\pi$)=Z, P($\\pi$/$2$)=S, dan P($\\pi/4$)=T. Sehingga fasa global $e^{i\\theta/2}$, ia bersamaan dengan RZ($\\theta$).\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"| Composer reference                              | OpenQASM reference | Q-sphere | Note about q-sphere representations                                                                                                                                                                                                     |\n"
"| ----------------------------------------------- | ------------------ | ---------------------------------------------------------------------- | --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n"
"| ![p\\_gate](/docs/images/guides/composer/2b9eec00-ecbf-45ce-ae09-8e3015dc6c98.avif) | `p(theta) q[0];`   | ![p\\_qsph](/docs/images/guides/composer/a02007e1-4c68-42af-b10c-49cbbaaed8ef.avif)                             | The q-sphere representation shows the state after the gate operates on the initial equal superposition state $\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2^{n}}}\\sum_{i=0}^{2^{n}-1}\\vert i\\rangle, $ where $n$ is the number of qubits needed to support the gate. |\n"
msgstr ""
"| Rujukan Composer                              | Rujukan OpenQASM | Q-sphere | Nota tentang representasi q-sphere                                                                                                                                                                                                     |\n"
"| ----------------------------------------------- | ------------------ | ---------------------------------------------------------------------- | --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n"
"| ![p\\_gate](/docs/images/guides/composer/2b9eec00-ecbf-45ce-ae09-8e3015dc6c98.avif) | `p(theta) q[0];`   | ![p\\_qsph](/docs/images/guides/composer/a02007e1-4c68-42af-b10c-49cbbaaed8ef.avif)                             | Representasi q-sphere menunjukkan keadaan selepas gate beroperasi pada keadaan superposisi sama rata awal $\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2^{n}}}\\sum_{i=0}^{2^{n}-1}\\vert i\\rangle, $ di mana $n$ ialah bilangan qubit yang diperlukan untuk menyokong gate. |\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "In IBM Quantum Composer, the default value for `theta` is $\\pi/2$.\n"
msgstr "Dalam IBM Quantum Composer, nilai lalai untuk `theta` ialah $\\pi/2$.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "**RZ gate**\n"
msgstr "**gate RZ**\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The RZ gate implements $exp(-i\\frac{\\theta}{2}Z)$. On the Bloch sphere, this gate corresponds to rotating the qubit state around the z axis by the given angle.\n"
msgstr "Gate RZ melaksanakan $exp(-i\\frac{\\theta}{2}Z)$. Pada sfera Bloch, gate ini sepadan dengan memutar keadaan qubit di sekitar paksi z mengikut sudut yang diberikan.\n"

