msgstr ""
"| Rujukan Composer                                    | Rujukan OpenQASM | Q-sphere | Nota tentang representasi q-sphere                                                                                                                                                                                                     |\n"
"| ----------------------------------------------------- | ------------------ | ---------------------------------------------------------------------- | --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n"
"| ![h-gate](/docs/images/guides/composer/fd58c6d3-f0af-4566-bf2b-105ed850c946.avif) | `h q[0];`          | ![image1](/docs/images/guides/composer/e797de24-e6de-44cb-9137-bb8931d763df.avif)                               | Representasi q-sphere menunjukkan keadaan selepas gate beroperasi pada keadaan superposisi sama rata awal $\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2^{n}}}\\sum_{i=0}^{2^{n}-1}\\vert i\\rangle, $ di mana $n$ ialah bilangan qubit yang diperlukan untuk menyokong gate. |\n"

#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Quantum gates {#quantum-gates}"
msgstr "gate quantum {#quantum-gates}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "**$\\sqrt{X}$ gate**\n"
msgstr "**gate $\\sqrt{X}$**\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Also known as the square-root NOT gate.\n"
msgstr "Juga dikenali sebagai gate square-root NOT.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "This gate implements the square-root of X, $\\sqrt{X}$. Applying this gate twice in a row produces the standard Pauli-X gate (NOT gate). Like the Hadamard gate, $\\sqrt{X}$ creates an equal superposition state if the qubit is in the state $|0\\rangle$, but with a different relative phase. On some hardwares, it is a native gate that can be implemented with a $\\pi/2$ or X90 pulse.\n"
msgstr "Gate ini melaksanakan punca kuasa dua X, $\\sqrt{X}$. Menggunakan gate ini dua kali berturut-turut menghasilkan gate Pauli-X piawai (gate NOT). Seperti gate Hadamard, $\\sqrt{X}$ mencipta keadaan superposisi sama rata jika qubit berada dalam keadaan $|0\\rangle$, tetapi dengan fasa relatif yang berbeza. Pada sesetengah perkakasan, ia adalah gate asli yang boleh dilaksanakan dengan denyutan $\\pi/2$ atau X90.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"| Composer reference                                | OpenQASM reference | Q-sphere | Note about q-sphere representations                                                                                                                                                                                                     |\n"
"| ------------------------------------------------- | ------------------ | ---------------------------------------------------------------------- | --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n"
"| ![sx\\_gate](/docs/images/guides/composer/67933b13-85f0-45e9-bc31-dcea4684dd6f.avif) | `sx q[0];`         | ![sx\\_qsph](/docs/images/guides/composer/fd300da1-512c-4193-8e77-b15e5e378d34.avif)                         | The q-sphere representation shows the state after the gate operates on the initial equal superposition state $\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2^{n}}}\\sum_{i=0}^{2^{n}-1}\\vert i\\rangle, $ where $n$ is the number of qubits needed to support the gate. |\n"
msgstr ""
"| Rujukan Composer                                | Rujukan OpenQASM | Q-sphere | Nota tentang representasi q-sphere                                                                                                                                                                                                     |\n"
"| ------------------------------------------------- | ------------------ | ---------------------------------------------------------------------- | --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n"
"| ![sx\\_gate](/docs/images/guides/composer/67933b13-85f0-45e9-bc31-dcea4684dd6f.avif) | `sx q[0];`         | ![sx\\_qsph](/docs/images/guides/composer/fd300da1-512c-4193-8e77-b15e5e378d34.avif)                         | Representasi q-sphere menunjukkan keadaan selepas gate beroperasi pada keadaan superposisi sama rata awal $\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2^{n}}}\\sum_{i=0}^{2^{n}-1}\\vert i\\rangle, $ di mana $n$ ialah bilangan qubit yang diperlukan untuk menyokong gate. |\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "**$\\sqrt{X}^{\\dagger}$ gate**\n"
msgstr "**gate $\\sqrt{X}^{\\dagger}$**\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Also known as the SXdg or square-root NOT-dagger gate.\n"
msgstr "Juga dikenali sebagai gate SXdg atau square-root NOT-dagger.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "This is the inverse of the $\\sqrt{X}$ gate. Applying it twice in a row produces the Pauli-X gate (NOT gate), since the NOT gate is its own inverse. Like the $\\sqrt{X}$ gate, this gate can be used to create an equal superposition state, and it too is natively implemented on some hardwares using an X90 pulse.\n"
msgstr "Ini adalah invers gate $\\sqrt{X}$. Menggunakannya dua kali berturut-turut menghasilkan gate Pauli-X (gate NOT), kerana gate NOT adalah inversnya sendiri. Seperti gate $\\sqrt{X}$, gate ini boleh digunakan untuk mencipta keadaan superposisi sama rata, dan ia juga dilaksanakan secara asli pada sesetengah perkakasan menggunakan denyutan X90.\n"

